# Local installation and verification

Verified tarball installed into npm global and fresh non-overwriting snapshot:
~/.local/share/ciel-runtime-1b08402a1da27fd13a870ddf5c8e0d11145d9f4c.
User CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME points to that snapshot. Version command reports the exact
nightly. Both snapshot and npm global match all 430 Python files in the tarball.
Installed focused tests: 372 run, zero failures/errors, 80 skipped.
Source native corrupt-history acceptance passed in run-claude-corrupt-history-v3-181742:
CLI alive while history corrupt; no send; owned fixture restoration then input
reply; no owned listeners after cleanup. Installed native acceptance
passed_corrupt_history_guard in run-claude-installed-history-guard-182944
passed the same corruption/no-send/recovery checks. Terminal text was captured;
the console HWND does not expose a usable window screenshot.

# Scope and limits

The previous release did not handle strict history errors at the polling
boundary and caused the startup crash seen on Celly. This release catches only
the typed pre-send condition, preserving the cursor and holding delivery. It
does not skip broken records or rewrite user history. Actual sandbox status
contents remain inaccessible (WinError 5); damaged row identity and origin are
unknown. Recovery of corrupted user history is not claimed.

No live session restart, sandbox install, ACL change, cursor rewrite, or queue
deletion was performed. Source and installed native testing uses owned fixtures.
